# Cursor Rules (legacy format — kept for older Cursor versions)
#
# The single source of truth is AI_CONTEXT.md at the repo root. Read it and
# follow it. Newer Cursor versions use .cursor/rules/project.mdc instead.

Follow AI_CONTEXT.md for project summary, tech stack, structure, and conventions.

- Match existing code style and .editorconfig; don't reformat unrelated code.
- Never hardcode secrets — use .env (gitignored).
- Don't add dependencies without team agreement; note any new dep in the PR.
- New features ship with at least one test.
- Update docs/CHANGELOG.md when behavior changes.
- If a requirement is unclear, leave a TODO: comment instead of guessing.
